From: hamza <hamza@book4>
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] usb: dwc3: prevent duplicate xHCI PHY management

DWC3 initializes and powers its generic PHYs before registering the xHCI
child. Set the existing XHCI_SKIP_PHY_INIT platform quirk so usb_add_hcd()
does not acquire another initialization and power reference to those PHYs
through hcd->self.sysdev.

On Book4, all three xHCI controllers have skip_phy_initialization=0 and a
non-NULL phy_roothub; the four USB3 PHYs each have init_count=power_count=2.
An awake runtime-PM test suspended xHCI and DWC3, but the selected PHY stayed
active with its clocks held. Root-hub autosuspend skips the non-auto PHY
suspend path, leaving its reference after DWC3 drops its own runtime vote.

Use the existing platform-data mechanism, shared by all DWC3 host children.
xHCI forwards the primary HCD's skip flag to the shared HCD. Include xhci.h
for the quirk definition; it already includes the three replaced headers.
This does not change runtime-PM defaults or wakeup policy.

The original fails the ownership regression. The corrected host object
compiles and the regression passes with the companion QMP correction.
This correction has not been booted or hardware-tested.
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
index 96b588bd0..8acfa3175 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c
@@ -13,9 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/usb.h>
 #include <linux/usb/hcd.h>
 
-#include "../host/xhci-port.h"
-#include "../host/xhci-ext-caps.h"
-#include "../host/xhci-caps.h"
+#include "../host/xhci.h"
 #include "../host/xhci-plat.h"
 #include "core.h"
 
@@ -78,6 +76,7 @@ static void dwc3_xhci_plat_start(struct usb_hcd *hcd)
 }
 
 static const struct xhci_plat_priv dwc3_xhci_plat_quirk = {
+	.quirks = XHCI_SKIP_PHY_INIT,
 	.plat_start = dwc3_xhci_plat_start,
 };
 
